    "updated_at": "2022-09-12T21:53:33Z",
    "body": "I got `0.003081 starship init zsh` but the delay is *noticeable*. Other timings also `0.00xx`. So it doesn't help much. \r\n\r\nIs there any way to have instantaneous mode such https://github.com/romkatv/powerlevel10k/blob/master/README.md#instant-prompt?\r\n\r\n### Update\r\n\r\nI use `zsh-defer` as suggested by p10k author here https://github.com/starship/starship/issues/407#issuecomment-573450759. But the delay is the same. No noticeable change.\r\n\r\n```diff\r\n-  source $ZDOTDIR/keybinds.zsh\r\n-  source $ZDOTDIR/completion.zsh\r\n-  source $ZDOTDIR/aliases.zsh\r\n-  source $ZDOTDIR/paths.zsh\r\n-  source $ZDOTDIR/apps.zsh\r\n+  zsh-defer $ZDOTDIR/keybinds.zsh\r\n+  zsh-defer $ZDOTDIR/completion.zsh\r\n+  zsh-defer $ZDOTDIR/aliases.zsh\r\n+  zsh-defer $ZDOTDIR/paths.zsh\r\n+  zsh-defer $ZDOTDIR/apps.zsh\r\n ```",
